---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend';
const title = 'Brevo vs Omnisend for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = 'Compare Brevo PushOwl and Omnisend for Shopify retail automation, wholesale sales boundaries, notification ownership and matched channel costs.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Brevo or Omnisend better for a Shopify store doing $40k/mo?",
    "answer": "Revenue alone does not decide the fit. Compare a Shopify welcome and recovery workflow in both. If wholesale sales already depend on Brevo, evaluate the cost of preserving that work alongside Omnisend against connecting Brevo PushOwl to the existing account."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does Brevo vs Omnisend pricing compare at 10,000 contacts?",
    "answer": "Use the same contact population, sends and channel destinations in both quotes. Include automation traffic, non-subscribed contacts where billable, retained sales tools and implementation. Entry prices do not answer a 10,000-contact question."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better Shopify integration?",
    "answer": "Both deserve an actual workflow rehearsal. Brevo documents PushOwl as its supported Shopify connector; Omnisend documents Shopify events for automation. Check the specific cart data, purchase exit and consent updates your store needs instead of assigning a universal integration winner."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I migrate from Brevo to Omnisend easily?",
    "answer": "Contact export is only part of migration. Inventory forms, suppression, event-dependent content and existing sales work. Rebuild a journey while sending is paused, prove purchase exits, then transfer its sending ownership. No fixed migration duration is promised."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which handles transactional email better?",
    "answer": "Omnisend supports order-confirmation automation, so it should not be excluded as marketing-only. Compare the exact notifications or API service you need and keep a sender map. Omnisend does not automatically disable Shopify confirmations; standard Shopify plans cannot fully disable the default order confirmation."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Omnisend push matter vs Brevo?",
    "answer": "Push can be useful if shoppers grant permission and the messages have a purpose distinct from email. Brevo PushOwl also supports web push. Compare permission collection, frequency and purchase exits; push availability alone does not decide this pairing."
  },
  {
    "question": "What workflow test should decide the winner?",
    "answer": "For a hybrid store, test a retail subscriber who later requests a wholesale quote. Can the operator pause consumer discounts while sales follows up, without losing legitimate order notifications? For a retail-only store, concentrate on product context, channel consent and stopping recovery after purchase. These are proposed tests, not reported results."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a> / Brevo vs Omnisend</nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head buyer guide</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Brevo vs Omnisend for Shopify email</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Should Shopify retention join an existing Brevo operation, or run in Omnisend alongside the sales tools you retain? The useful distinction is who operates each customer journey, especially when the same person buys at retail and negotiates wholesale.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl"><TldrBox picks={[
      { label: 'Existing Brevo team', tool: 'Brevo PushOwl', reason: 'Evaluate connecting Shopify without discarding established customer work.' },
      { label: 'Retail automation team', tool: 'Omnisend', reason: 'Evaluate Shopify event-driven email, SMS and push in one workflow.' },
    ]} /></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Start with the actual Shopify connections</h2>
      <p><a href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Brevo’s setup guide</a> identifies PushOwl as the supported Shopify connection and describes email, SMS and web push. An existing Brevo account can be connected. The question is whether adding store data helps the team preserve useful customer work without creating conflicting permissions. Brevo should not be dismissed as lacking push or ecommerce automation.</p>
      <p><a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/4298431-understand-event-data-in-automation-workflows">Omnisend’s event-data guide</a> describes using store events and their details in automation messages. This is useful when a retail marketer wants order or cart context within a multichannel journey. It does not establish faster implementation, better recovery or a replacement for every sales process.</p>
      <h2>Separate three jobs before comparing features</h2>
      <table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Decision to make</th><th>Evidence to collect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Retail retention</td><td>Which workspace owns welcome, recovery and repeat-purchase messaging?</td><td>Event record, rendered product content and purchase exit for each journey.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wholesale follow-up</td><td>Where does a salesperson manage a quote and the next action?</td><td>Named owner, current deal record and handoff from a retail profile.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Order service</td><td>Which sender delivers each receipt or shipment notice?</td><td>Paid and fulfilled test orders with a complete message log.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
      <p>A single platform is valuable if it removes a real handoff. Two platforms can be workable if each has a clear responsibility. Do not migrate sales work merely because the retail team prefers another editor; equally, do not retain an unused sales module to justify a suite subscription.</p>
      <h2>Proposed hybrid-store rehearsal: retail buyer becomes a wholesale lead</h2>
      <p>Use a permitted test profile to join a retail signup form, place a small order and then submit a wholesale inquiry using the same address. Record the retail subscription separately from the sales request. Assign a sales owner and an explicit wholesale-pending status. Before enabling a consumer winback offer, decide whether that status should exclude the profile or route it to a different message.</p>
      <p>Ask the salesperson to close the inquiry without buying, then reopen it after another retail order. Does the status remain understandable? Can the marketer explain why a consumer discount was withheld? The required evidence is a traceable profile and message history, not a presumed percentage uplift. A wholesale request is not permission for every promotional channel.</p>
      <p>For a Brevo-plus-Omnisend arrangement, specify how the retail workspace learns that the sales conversation is active. If that handoff requires manual updates, record its owner and failure handling. Connecting both products to Shopify alone does not prove that a sales status crosses between them. If no reliable handoff exists, limit the initial scope rather than assuming shared identity means shared eligibility.</p>
      <h2>Proposed retail-only rehearsal: a purchase between channel steps</h2>
      <p>Create a recoverable cart with a recognizable product and enter the draft workflow. Check the email’s item, link and currency. Purchase before the next scheduled step, then inspect whether email, SMS and push all stop as intended. Repeat with email permission only, then with the additional channel permissions your store actually collects. A contact being reachable by email says nothing about permission or reachability on another channel.</p>
      <p>Record event arrival and workflow evaluation separately. Delayed sync, a missing identity and a wrong exit condition need different fixes. Choose a tolerable delay from the planned customer experience rather than importing a universal ten-minute threshold. These rehearsals are proposed; this guide reports no store tests or recovery results.</p>
      <h2>Protect existing permissions during the Brevo connection</h2>
      <p>Brevo warns that the initial Shopify import can overwrite existing contact attributes, including subscription status. Before connecting an established sales account, preserve an export and review conflicting records: opted out in Brevo but subscribed in Shopify, sales-only contacts and customers with no promotional permission. Keep marketing paused while reconciling those cases. Review ongoing consent settings separately; a successful initial import does not prove future updates behave as intended.</p>
      <h2>Order confirmations are a separate decision</h2>
      <p><a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/1421803-order-confirmation-automation">Omnisend documents order-confirmation workflows</a> and warns that Shopify’s own confirmation is not automatically disabled. Its guide distinguishes standard Shopify plans, where the default confirmation cannot be fully disabled, from Plus. Decide whether an additional message adds useful information before activating it.</p>
      <p>Inventory confirmation, fulfillment, refund and custom application messages individually. Retaining Shopify notifications may be the simplest initial boundary. Installing Brevo PushOwl does not itself establish a replacement for custom transactional API work. If that work already exists, include its templates, credentials, monitoring and owner in the migration scope. Do not infer that either vendor must replace every service message.</p>
      <h2>Compare the same workload rather than entry prices</h2>
      <p><a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/3533018-omnisend-pricing-plans-2026">Omnisend’s pricing documentation</a> distinguishes billable contacts, email credits and plan limits. <a href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/208589409-About-Brevo-s-pricing-plans">Brevo’s plan guide</a> describes tiers and add-ons. Obtain dated quotes for your imported population, required features and peak sending; this page supplies no supplier price estimate.</p>
      <p>Hypothetical workload: 6,000 eligible retail subscribers receiving five campaigns create 30,000 emails. Add 4,000 welcome and recovery emails for 34,000 marketing emails. If you separately forecast 2,500 order-service emails, the total is 36,500, but whether those share a quota depends on the quoted setup. Add SMS by destination and message segments, and push by the applicable plan. Keep sales follow-up volume visible rather than silently folding it into the retail list.</p>
      <p>For an illustrative operating comparison, suppose one setup costs $60 more each month but saves two hours valued internally at $35 per hour. The estimated labor saving is $70, leaving $10 before migration costs. These are invented planning inputs, not vendor prices or measured savings. Replace them with timed work by your operator and a quote; no recovery revenue is assumed.</p>
      <h2>Migration and go-live responsibilities</h2>
      <p>Export active journeys, forms, suppression rules and the sales processes you intend to retain. Rebuild one journey while sending is paused. Check consent conflicts and purchase exits before handing that journey to the new sender. Do not leave two live recovery sequences targeting the same cart. Keep a rollback record of which sender was paused and what must be restored.</p>
      <p>Ask a second operator to locate an unexpected enrollment, change a discount exclusion and explain the next send. Record actual work time and unresolved dependencies. There is no universal two-week migration or mandatory ninety-day trial: the scope is complete when the required journeys and handoffs have evidence, with remaining gaps assigned to an owner.</p>
      <h2>Decision for this pairing</h2>
      <p>For an established Brevo sales team, first compare the effort of connecting PushOwl with the effort of moving retail messaging while preserving sales work. For a retail-focused team, give Omnisend a full event-and-channel rehearsal alongside Brevo PushOwl. Favor the setup that meets the required journeys with affordable, explainable operations. Neither revenue level, channel count nor an invented recovery benchmark supplies a universal winner.</p>
    </article>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm"><p class="font-black">Related comparisons</p><p class="mt-2">
      <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-mailchimp">Brevo vs Mailchimp</a> ·
      <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo vs Omnisend</a> ·
      <a class="link" href="/for/b2b-wholesale">Email apps for B2B wholesale</a>
    </p></div>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Brevo vs Omnisend FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
